CAVEAT:  The case was written for an XS916MXT master and an XS916MXS member. This run used an
         IE520 4-member stack. Traffic entered the master (member 3) and left member 4, so it
         crossed the stack. The hourly reads were made by tools/longrun.py, not a TeraTerm
         macro. Memory was read once per hour, so a change shorter than one hour can fall
         between two reads.
